metalive wrote:

> Hey guys, I think I have discovered this puzzle level 'Sokoban'! It
> starts at Dlvl 6 and goes upwards. I've completed the first level but
> messed up the second.
> Is it compulsory to do Sokoban?

No. But there is an amulet of reflection *or* a bag of holding if you
manage to do all four levels.

If you have to 'cheat' to finish a level, beware! Every 'cheat' costs you
one point of luck (which is measured on a scale of -10 to +10, normally),
and it may take a long time to restore your luck.

> Because on Dlvl 6 I can't find a way down to Dlvl 7. There are only
> two stairs up, one to Dlvl 5 and the other up to Dlvl5-Sokoban. Am
> I forever stuck?

As said before by me and others: you're wrong. There *is* a way down to
level 7. You just can't find it. Why don't you believe us?

Why don't you go back up and look for a level with two staircases down?
One of these should be the entrance to the Gnomish Mines. You should be
able to find a pickaxe there, and use that to continue your search for
other rooms on level 6.

Alternatively, and this may be a lot quicker, you can (k)ick every wall on
level 6 (stop kicking when you've hurt yourself). When you get to the spot
where there's a secret door that (s)earching didn't reveal, you'll kick it
open.

> Another question: My cat fell through a hole a while ago and I can't
> find him anymore... What will happen to him? Poor thing... :-(

It will have fallen one or two levels down, normally. If you don't get to
that level yourself within a few hunderd moves, it will lose its tameness.

By the way, if it fell down on level 6, you can use that hole as well to
reach level 7 or 8. If it fell down on level 5, you can use that hole
(repeatedly, if necessary) to reach the undiscovered parts of level 6 or
get to level 7 directly.

Hope this helps.

